{
  "slug": "clean-code-assistant",
  "name": "Clean Code Assistant",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Enforces clean code principles across your project and fixes the code for you - not just flags\nwhat's wrong. Ships with 14 plain-language rules (formal textbook names in parentheses for experts),\n13 skills, a background reviewer agent that appends non-blocking suggestions after every edit, and\na plan-mode hook that reminds Claude to factor clean code into every plan. Every detection skill\nsupports both report-only mode and a fix mode that applies the changes directly. Multi-platform:\ngenerates matching configs for Cursor (.cursorrules) and Codex CLI (AGENTS.md) from one source of\ntruth. Based on Code Complete 2nd Ed., The Art of Clean Code, and OOP vs. Functional Programming.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **14 skills**, **1 agent** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (14): `analyze` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"analyze this file\", \"check this code\", \"scan for…), `fix` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"fix everything\", \"fix all violations\", \"clean this up\",…), `health` (This skill should be used when the user asks for \"project health\", \"code health\", \"clean code score\", \"cleanliness…), `init` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"set up clean code rules\", \"initialize clean code\",…), `refactor` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"refactor this file\", \"clean up this code\", \"extract…), `restructure` (Extract misplaced code from any folder (backend or frontend) and move it to a properly-named folder that fits…), `rewrite` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"clean my code\", \"make it human readable\", \"make…), `safety` (This skill should be used when the user asks to \"check error handling\", \"find silent failures\", \"fix silent…), and 6 more\n- **Agents** (1): `cleancode-reviewer` (Use this agent after writing or editing code to silently review it for clean code violations)\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install clean-code-assistant@claude-community` from `DinoQuinten/cleancode-assistant` (`cleancode`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 14,
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 2
  },
